{
  "_comment": "MarginIQ project registry. Add a new platform by adding an entry under 'projects' - no code change needed. 'param_aliases' maps a log's START_RMT header name to the tool's canonical parameter name (e.g. WCL prints RxVref where NVL prints RxDqVrefByte). 'rmt_fallback_markers' (optional) lists extra block markers (e.g. WCL START_BYTE_RMT) parsed ONLY when a log has no START_RMT data and only inside 'Rank Margin Tool' task runs. 'require_rmt_task' (optional, default false) = RMT data is taken ONLY from inside the 'Rank Margin Tool' MRC task; a log without it (or with an empty task) is reported with a NO RMT DATA warning and skipped, so per-training-step Composite-UI blocks are never plotted. 'platform_variants' (optional) maps the memory family decoded from the log (DDR5 / LPDDR5) to a platform variant label shown in the Platform tab and PPT. 'dtr' (optional) overrides the thermal DTR parsing: layout 'rmt_task_runs' = Boot RMT is the first 'Rank Margin Tool' run and Run RMT the last, 'rmt_markers' = accepted block start markers, 'temps_from_filename' = Boot/Run temps from BCRH (0/90) or BHRC (90/0) in the file name. Projects without 'dtr' use the built-in NVL flow (Temp Drift RMT Test + Hit Enter + PHY Temperature1). 'axis_config' is the default Y-axis JSON for that project (relative to the repo root). 'rmt_limits' (optional) = spec pass/fail limits per memory family (DDR5 / LPDDR5, decoded from the log) and frequency (read from the log): used as the +/-Ref lines in JMP / HTML / PPT and for the spec PASS/FAIL table; nearest listed frequency is used (with a warning) when the exact one is missing. Disable with --no-rmt-limits.",
